# **IPD‑12 Capture Validation Schema**  
### *JSON Schema Draft‑07 — Validates all capture objects produced by map_process()*

```json
{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "title": "IPD-12 Capture Object",
  "description": "Validation schema for RTT-IPD-12 process capture.",
  "type": "object",

  "required": [
    "name",
    "purpose",
    "boundaries",
    "structural_layers",
    "operational_flow",
    "coherence_baseline",
    "domain",
    "regime_level"
  ],

  "properties": {
    "name": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "description": "Canonical identifier of the process."
    },

    "purpose": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "description": "Primary intent or goal of the process."
    },

    "boundaries": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": { "type": "string" },
      "description": "Constraints, limits, or scope of the process."
    },

    "structural_layers": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": { "type": "string" },
      "description": "Major structural components of the process."
    },

    "operational_flow": {
      "type": "array",
      "minItems": 1,
      "items": { "type": "string" },
      "description": "Sequence or topology of operations."
    },

    "coherence_baseline": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "description": "Definition of what counts as coherent or aligned."
    },

    "domain": {
      "type": "string",
      "minLength": 1,
      "description": "Domain classification (music, physics, workflow, etc.)."
    },

    "regime_level": {
      "type": "string",
      "enum": ["surface", "mid", "deep"],
      "description": "RTT regime level; IPD-12 supports up to deep."
    }
  }
}
```

---

## **Why this schema matters**

This validation schema enforces the **capture → drift contract**:

- No drift without capture  
- No tensor without layered capture  
- No coherence without a baseline  
- No paradox without declared anchors  

It ensures every `map_process()` output is structurally complete and ready for:

```
drift()
detect_divergence()
drift_tensor()
align_coherence()
cross_system()
```

